# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the tests of PBeFS.
#
# The single-producer single-consumer queues of FastFlow are lock-free by
# design: they read and write the slots and the indices without atomic
# operations, ordering them with explicit memory barriers, which
# ThreadSanitizer does not understand. Only the internals of FastFlow are
# suppressed, so that the code of the library that uses them is checked.
race:ff::SWSR_Ptr_Buffer
race:ff::uSWSR_Ptr_Buffer
race:ff::Buffer_
race:ff::ff_node
race:ff::ff_thread
race:ff::ff_loadbalancer
race:ff::ff_gatherer
#
# Lace, the scheduler of Sylvan, hands its tasks and their results over with
# fences, which ThreadSanitizer does not model, and Sylvan shares its table
# of the nodes and its cache of the operations without locks, the cache
# checked by a hash: every value that crosses a worker of Lace reads as a
# race. Only the races whose first frame is in Lace (its functions, and the
# functions that its macros generate for each task: _SPAWN, _SYNC,
# _SYNC_SLOW, _WRAP, _RUN) or in Sylvan are suppressed; the results that the
# tasks of PBeFS leave to other threads are published with release and
# acquire [see src/Bdd.cpp], so that its own code stays checked.
race_top:^lace_*
race_top:*_SPAWN$
race_top:*_SYNC$
race_top:*_SYNC_SLOW$
race_top:*_WRAP$
race_top:*_RUN$
race_top:^cache_get$
race_top:^cache_put$
race_top:^llmsset_*
race_top:^mtbddnode_*
race_top:^mtbdd_*
race_top:^sylvan_*
